{"id": "EUVD-2026-104304", "enisaUuid": "84773b3d-4bac-3444-9870-521a92baecfe", "description": "SGLang through 0.5.22 with the Mooncake disaggregation backend accepts unauthenticated decode registration messages on the Prefill rank ZMQ PULL socket, allowing denial of service. Network-adjacent attackers can send many registrations with unique mooncake_session_id values and large nested-buffer frames to exhaust Prefill memory until the scheduler is OOM-killed.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:06:43", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/issues/45012", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/mooncake/conn.py#L2885-L2935", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/mooncake/conn.py#L889-L909", "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/v0.5.22/python/sglang/srt/disaggregation/common/utils.py#L47-L69", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/sglang-through-0.5.22-memory-exhaustion-via-unauthenticated-mooncake-decode-registrations"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112269", "GHSA-9qhw-7fv2-2hgm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8a8edd24-fa00-3f03-8156-29b944716b12", "product": {"name": "sglang", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.22"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3ee5d601-27cb-3d4b-a4d5-621f933a3edc", "vendor": {"name": "sgl-project"}}], "isExploited": false}